course: dictionary
lesson: 10901
title: Visibility
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Visibility is a noun. It tells you how far or how clearly you can see. In thick fog, you cannot see far, so the visibility is poor. You can see a word's clues in the words around it: «Hard hats protect heads from falling things, and hi-vis vests make workers easy to see; hi-vis means high visibility.» The clue is easy to see, so visibility must mean how easy something is to see.
explain: Visibility can also mean how much people know about or notice something. A campaign raises visibility when more people hear about it. You can check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Visibility means how far or how clearly you can see.
fact: Visibility can also mean how easy something is to see or notice.
fact: «Poor visibility» means you cannot see very far, for example in fog.
fact: «High-visibility» (hi-vis) clothes are bright so people can see you easily.
exercise: «Hard hats protect heads from falling things, and hi-vis vests make workers easy to see.» What does hi-vis mean? | Very loud | Hidden from view | Very high hats | *High visibility, easy to see
exercise: The sign on the motorway said «poor visibility» because of thick fog. What does poor visibility mean? | You can see the stars clearly | Everyone can see the sign easily | The road is very wide | *You cannot see very far
exercise: The charity wanted to raise visibility for its new project. What does raising visibility mean? | *Helping more people notice and know about it | Making the project cheaper | Making it harder to find | Making the charity smaller
test: Why do road workers wear hi-vis vests? | *So drivers and others can see them easily | To look like famous people | To keep their hands dry | To keep warm in the cold
test: A driver sees «visibility is down to fifty metres» on the radio. What should the driver do in fog? | Speed up to get home | Stop listening to the radio | Turn off all lights | *Drive slowly and use lights
exam: The radio says «visibility is down to twenty metres» because of fog. What does this tell you? | Everyone can see every car easily | Drivers can see the sky very clearly | The fog has finished | *You can only see about twenty metres ahead
